WEBVTT

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:14.860
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:15.070
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:37.990
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:44.500
<b>Chapter One     White Meeting</b>

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:01.010
<i>2015, summer.</i>

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:01.010
<b>2015   Summer</b>

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:04.770
<i>I offer this diary to you.</i>

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:07.820
<i>To tell you</i>

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:10.270
<i>what she was thinking,</i>

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:13.840
<i>and what her fate was.</i>

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:21.530
<i>She was always thinking...</i>

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:24.020
<i>About who she was,</i>

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:25.720
<i>where she'd come from,</i>

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:27.350
<i>and where she was going.</i>

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:32.160
<i>Everyone convinces themselves 
that life is an enjoyable thing.</i>

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:34.480
<i>She, however,</i>

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:38.850
<i>was always thinking about how 
much of a burden it was.</i>

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:42.680
<i>And about how much of our freedom</i>

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:46.220
<i>was lost by the conviction that</i>

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:50.720
<i>we had to stay alive.</i>

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:09.830
Miss, it's about time to leave.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:14.840
I know, Suwano.

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:44.250
Okay, bye!

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:46.620
Goodbye, miss.

00:04:30.110 --> 00:04:32.710
Good morning, Saikawa-sensei.

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:35.210
Morning, Nishinosono-kun.

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:38.340
You seem tired, Sensei.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:39.920
How can you tell?

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:42.060
That's easy.

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:45.270
When you're feeling good, you put 
coffee on first thing, right?

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:48.470
The only time you drink soda from the can

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:51.680
is when you're tired and don't want to do anything.

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:54.880
I see. You're a careful observer.

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:02.610
It's an elephant today, huh?

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:06.040
Where do you get those T-shirts?

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:08.850
Just tell me already!

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:16.250
Nishinosono-kun, let me give you some life advice.

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:17.650
Yes?

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:20.740
Never tell others what you're really thinking.

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:23.490
So there was a committee meeting, huh?

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:25.070
You're sharp.

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:29.280
Naturally, what was supposed to be a 
one-hour meeting took three hours,

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:30.710
as I expected.

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:33.350
Because so many people are stupid.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:36.270
No, because enough aren't stupid.

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:40.400
These are all people who don't want 
to be thought of as stupid.

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:43.030
Isn't that because they are stupid?

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:45.650
Well, I guess you could say that.

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:48.430
You're feeling a little better now, aren't you?

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:50.520
I'm forcing myself to feel better.

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:53.040
Oh, you're lying to me, aren't you?

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:56.930
In life, there are three great questions.

00:05:56.930 --> 00:06:00.040
Who am I? Where do I come from?

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:01.570
Where am I going?

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:04.390
That's all I want to think about.

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:07.940
Honestly, thought is the 
one thing that is truly free.

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:09.670
However,

00:06:09.670 --> 00:06:13.090
at some point, this strange power 
started controlling me,

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:16.280
and it began to be more complicated and less free.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:21.540
When I was a kid, I'm sure I was able
 to think more freely about many things.

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:25.010
I guess humans

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:27.790
are programmed to get stupider as they age.

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:31.520
You're not stupid.

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:34.330
But I am getting older.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:36.510
Just like the way your hair gets longer.

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:39.390
Oh, do you like it longer?

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:40.780
No comment.

00:06:41.240 --> 00:06:45.520
Sensei, it's fine to talk about complicated stuff,

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:48.560
but you should take me
 somewhere once in a while!

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:49.930
Somewhere?

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:54.330
There's a new cake roll place in 
front of Kakuouzan Station...

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:57.640
They say the cakes are really soft and delicious!

00:06:58.200 --> 00:06:59.390
When do you want to go?

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:01.480
I'm bad with promises.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:03.060
Why?

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:05.630
Whenever I get up in the morning,

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:08.190
I always think to myself,

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:10.890
"Am I really the same person I was yesterday?"

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:14.060
You are to me.

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:18.350
For example,

00:07:18.350 --> 00:07:22.080
just as a computer loads its OS into memory, 
and boots up each time it restarts,

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:26.760
is it possible I'm just booting up the person 
called "Saikawa Sohei" each morning,

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:29.450
and trying to play that role?

00:07:29.450 --> 00:07:32.800
So? In other words, you won't take me on a date?

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:35.270
We were talking about a date?

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:36.390
Jeez!

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:39.220
You're an expert at changing 
the subject, aren't you?

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:44.970
Excuse me, Saikawa-sensei...

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:48.350
Oh, Nishinosono-san, you're here again?

00:07:48.350 --> 00:07:49.230
Hi.

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:50.950
What is it, Hamanaka-kun?

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:54.240
My computer's acting weird.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:56.100
Can you take a look at it?

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:57.930
Kunieda-kun isn't there?

00:07:58.610 --> 00:08:01.210
It looks like it's kind of a bad time right now...

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:02.700
I understand.

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:07.210
In her case, it's probably difficult 
to find a good time.

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:12.210
I know, right?

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:17.560
Hold on a second, Nishinosono-kun.

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:18.740
Sure.

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:20.140
Oh, so, Sensei...

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:22.700
Where are we going for our seminar trip this year?

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:25.800
This year, I'm in charge of it.

00:08:31.630 --> 00:08:32.780
What is your name?

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:34.550
Nishinosono.

00:08:34.850 --> 00:08:36.520
I know your last name.

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:37.770
What is your name?

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:39.150
Moe.

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:41.790
Written with the kanji for 
"growing grass" and "colorful paints."

00:08:42.150 --> 00:08:43.200
How old are you?

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:45.150
Almost twenty.

00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:47.670
Um... Dr. Magata?

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:49.420
You knew my father, right—

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:53.200
What is 165 multiplied by 3,367?

00:08:54.280 --> 00:08:57.870
555,555...

00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:00.130
It appears you're bad at multiplying sevens.

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:02.370
That's not true.

00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:04.300
I like the number seven.

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:06.930
Seven is a special number, isn't it?

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:10.380
It's the only lonely number.

00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:12.600
What do you mean?

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:16.140
Try dividing the numbers one 
through ten into two groups.

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:20.800
And then multiply all of the 
numbers within each group.

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:24.540
Is it possible for the resulting sums to be equal?

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:25.900
No.

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:28.680
One of the groups contains a seven,

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:31.070
so the sum will be a multiple of seven.

00:09:31.390 --> 00:09:34.870
But there's no seven in the other. 
So they can't be equal.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:38.050
See? Seven is the only lonely number, isn't it?

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:40.410
B and D are the same way.

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:43.520
Is it true that you killed your parents?

00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:46.380
Your brain works fast.

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:48.260
And you're decisive.

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:52.950
He told you to meet with me, right?

00:09:53.500 --> 00:09:54.850
"He"?

00:09:54.850 --> 00:09:56.720
Saikawa-sensei.

00:09:57.570 --> 00:10:00.850
No... I came here on my own.

00:10:00.850 --> 00:10:02.940
I came because I'm interested in you.

00:10:02.940 --> 00:10:05.660
I lied about wanting to hear about my father.

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:08.250
You are a very honest girl, aren't you?

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:13.020
You were raised in a wealthy family.

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:15.600
Was your father very strict?

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:17.810
And... Hmm...

00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:20.920
You are attracted to Saikawa-sensei, aren't you?

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:26.550
Saikawa-sensei was my father's last student.

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:29.870
A brilliant man, with a very innovative 
method of thinking.

00:10:29.870 --> 00:10:30.780
He is worthy of respect—

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:32.270
That is not an answer.

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:37.030
The answer is yes.

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:43.160
Sohei-kun?

00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:48.200
Oh, sorry.

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:50.180
Are you a student?

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:54.020
Yes, Saikawa-sensei will be back soon.

00:10:54.020 --> 00:10:55.100
Oh.

00:10:55.100 --> 00:10:58.300
Then could you give this to him?

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:01.720
Um, who are you?

00:11:04.130 --> 00:11:07.820
Are you Nishinosono-san?

00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:13.000
I am Nishinosono, but...

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:14.690
Excuse me, who are you?

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:16.900
I'm...

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:20.020
Gido Setsuko!

00:11:20.020 --> 00:11:21.740
Gido-san?

00:11:25.050 --> 00:11:26.150
Is there a problem?

00:11:26.150 --> 00:11:28.820
You should grow out your hair.

00:11:28.820 --> 00:11:30.570
It'd look good on you...

00:11:33.310 --> 00:11:35.920
So you're Nishinosono-san, huh?

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:39.010
Uh, how do you know me?

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:41.100
Because all Sohei-kun

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:43.720
ever talks about is you.

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:47.170
Um, how are you and he connected—

00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:48.440
Sorry.

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:50.210
I've got a taxi outside.

00:11:50.210 --> 00:11:52.940
Tell Sohei-kun I said, "Hi."

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:54.250
Ciao!

00:11:59.430 --> 00:12:01.650
Sorry, Nishinosono-kun.

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:02.470
Not at all.

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:04.030
Is something wrong?

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:05.770
No, nothing.

00:12:06.130 --> 00:12:08.350
You had a visitor just now.

00:12:12.890 --> 00:12:13.830
Who?

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:15.640
Someone named Gido-san.

00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:17.410
She left immediately.

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:19.570
And she said to give you this.

00:12:19.950 --> 00:12:21.670
All right. Thanks.

00:12:23.780 --> 00:12:25.180
You're mad, aren't you?

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:26.490
Not at all.

00:12:26.790 --> 00:12:28.100
You can eat one of those.

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:29.300
I know that.

00:12:32.860 --> 00:12:34.370
This is horrible...

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:37.190
Nishinosono-kun, you know this, right?

00:12:37.450 --> 00:12:40.570
There are three things in this world 
that I simply cannot eat.

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:42.380
Red bean jam, roasted soy flour—

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:43.530
Watermelon.

00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:45.530
She's just screwing with me.

00:12:45.960 --> 00:12:46.990
This is infuriating.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:50.290
Nishinosono-kun, want to do some coloring books?

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:51.330
Coloring books?

00:12:51.710 --> 00:12:52.910
That was a joke.

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:55.140
Luxury means something with no meaning at all.

00:12:57.320 --> 00:12:59.360
You're still angry, aren't you?

00:12:59.820 --> 00:13:01.600
But those feelings are

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:05.950
an uncertain thing, like a crystal 
on the verge of collapse.

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:09.840
Sure, just sit there, sounding cool, Sensei.

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:12.750
You had something you wanted to say to me, right?

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:15.090
No...

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:17.540
I mean, I do!

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:19.320
What is it? Go ahead.

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:20.620
I...

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:28.170
went to Magata Labs.

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:31.150
And? Were you able to meet Dr. Magata Shiki?

00:13:31.150 --> 00:13:33.030
What's wrong?

00:13:33.030 --> 00:13:35.570
The tone of your voice just went up.

00:13:36.150 --> 00:13:37.610
You're imagining it...

00:13:37.610 --> 00:13:40.690
She knew you.

00:13:40.690 --> 00:13:42.460
She's read your papers, it seems.

00:13:42.970 --> 00:13:43.960
Really?

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:46.850
Don't just show your teeth like that!

00:13:46.850 --> 00:13:48.940
No, I mean...

00:13:48.940 --> 00:13:49.690
Excuse me.

00:13:49.690 --> 00:13:51.400
I'm sorry! Right now, I'm—

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:52.980
Sorry.

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:56.960
Like we thought, the problem with 
the computer was a virus.

00:13:57.820 --> 00:13:58.970
Thanks.

00:13:59.390 --> 00:14:01.160
How's your seminar going?

00:14:01.660 --> 00:14:02.940
Terribly.

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:05.400
They still aren't using their brains.

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:07.640
Romance is the only thing on their minds.

00:14:10.790 --> 00:14:12.290
I'm hungry.

00:14:12.290 --> 00:14:14.570
I'll treat you somewhere, Nishinosono-kun.

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:20.830
Why not go with him?

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:22.180
Right!

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:29.010
What does Gido-san do?

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:30.300
Sensei?

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:32.260
I'm sorry. Hold on a second...

00:14:39.160 --> 00:14:41.200
You're as terrible at that as ever.

00:14:42.070 --> 00:14:43.610
Thanks.

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:45.530
She's an interesting girl, isn't she?

00:14:45.770 --> 00:14:48.340
"I don't want to talk about something so stupid."

00:14:49.710 --> 00:14:51.270
That's what you're thinking, isn't it?

00:14:51.980 --> 00:14:52.910
You are sharp.

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:56.790
Dr. Magata was really pretty.

00:14:57.170 --> 00:14:59.430
I heard she was twenty-nine,

00:14:59.430 --> 00:15:01.420
but she looked a lot younger.

00:15:01.830 --> 00:15:04.860
She was wearing all white, even her gloves.

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:07.550
And it was like...

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:10.900
She was like an angel
that didn't belong in this world.

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:13.860
But sometimes, she looked like a devil.

00:15:14.830 --> 00:15:18.520
Well, we were only able to talk via video chat.

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:23.310
I heard her new interview with <i>Times</i> 
magazine was the same way.

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:25.550
You know all about her, huh?

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:27.380
For the past three years,

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:31.380
she's started appearing in the public eye.

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:32.070
But...

00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:34.910
Why would she meet someone like me?

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:37.360
I was sure she'd refuse.

00:15:37.850 --> 00:15:40.330
She got stupid, too...

00:15:40.950 --> 00:15:44.080
Stupid enough to finally take an interest in others.

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:46.650
In her interview, she said the same thing.

00:15:47.240 --> 00:15:49.980
"Every human starts as a genius.

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:52.840
And as they age, they become average.

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:56.490
It's because they get stupid that they can work.

00:15:56.490 --> 00:15:58.310
They can make small talk."

00:15:59.460 --> 00:16:02.080
That sounds like something you'd say.

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:04.610
Oh, what a coincidence!

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:06.900
Am I interrupting?

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:07.810
Not at all.

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:11.110
Sorry!

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:12.500
Saikawa-sensei,

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:15.690
about this year's seminar trip...

00:16:15.690 --> 00:16:18.550
We need to decide where we're goi—

00:16:17.610 --> 00:16:18.550
Hamanaka-kun...

00:16:18.850 --> 00:16:22.400
Nishinosono-kun said she met with Dr. Magata.

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:24.360
Dr. Magata?

00:16:24.660 --> 00:16:26.310
The genius programmer?

00:16:26.310 --> 00:16:27.560
How did you pull that off?

00:16:27.560 --> 00:16:29.570
I asked my aunt.

00:16:30.520 --> 00:16:33.790
Your aunt is, uh...

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:35.510
The wife of the governor of Aichi Prefecture.

00:16:35.850 --> 00:16:39.070
Then your dad used to be

00:16:39.070 --> 00:16:41.000
the president of our college?!

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:42.180
And she's his little sister.

00:16:43.810 --> 00:16:44.900
Wow.

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:49.900
Dr. Magata earned her doctorate 
in her teens, right?

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:52.600
When she was eleven, to be precise.

00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:56.070
At age twelve, she began to work as an engineer.

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:59.590
And her name's still known in a variety of fields.

00:17:00.170 --> 00:17:02.910
The only person I know

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:06.250
who can legitimately be called a genius is Dr. Magata.

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:10.120
But she's a criminal, right?

00:17:10.120 --> 00:17:11.530
A long time ago, she—

00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:14.760
Fifteen years ago, Magata Shiki

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:18.430
killed her parents, who also held doctorates.

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:20.720
I asked about that, too.

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:22.220
What did she say?

00:17:22.830 --> 00:17:24.780
That a doll killed them.

00:17:25.370 --> 00:17:27.320
A doll did it.

00:17:27.320 --> 00:17:29.860
I saw it happen.

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:33.270
A doll committed the murders?

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:38.370
I am aware, of course, that no one believes this.

00:17:38.730 --> 00:17:40.710
But the truth exists,

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:42.940
regardless of others' understanding of it.

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:44.410
And she said

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:47.370
that doll disappeared somewhere...

00:17:47.770 --> 00:17:49.880
After the incident,

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:52.820
Magata Shiki was declared <i>non compos mentis</i>,

00:17:52.820 --> 00:17:54.880
and therefore not guilty.

00:17:55.250 --> 00:17:58.760
And afterward, she vanished.

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:01.100
But in fact,

00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:06.490
she'd gone to a lab on
 Himaka Island, in Mikawa Bay.

00:18:06.940 --> 00:18:11.480
This whole time, she's been 
conducting her research there.

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:16.400
Then the rumor was true?

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:19.940
I see... You were able to meet her?

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:23.310
I wish I could, at least, send her an e-mail.

00:18:23.310 --> 00:18:26.160
Would you feel the same way

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:27.580
if she were a man, Sensei?

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:29.840
That's a stupid question, Nishinosono-kun.

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:34.250
I don't know how many scientists 
there are in the world right now,

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:39.080
but I don't think any of them wouldn't 
want to meet Dr. Magata.

00:18:39.500 --> 00:18:41.560
Even you, known as "the hope of academia,"

00:18:41.560 --> 00:18:44.560
who's received every award he possibly could?

00:18:44.880 --> 00:18:46.260
Of course.

00:18:46.550 --> 00:18:48.330
Everything I've done in my life

00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:50.870
wouldn't amount to the toenail on her little toe.

00:18:51.490 --> 00:18:53.670
Do you want to meet her?

00:18:54.170 --> 00:18:55.090
Yes.

00:18:55.090 --> 00:18:56.110
Why?

00:18:56.350 --> 00:18:59.130
If I met her, I might be able to escape.

00:18:59.130 --> 00:19:00.240
From where?

00:19:01.190 --> 00:19:02.620
From this world.

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:04.830
So let's go to Himaka Island!

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:06.630
The seminar trip.

00:19:06.630 --> 00:19:07.960
Let's all go.

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:10.450
There's a campground on that island!

00:19:10.450 --> 00:19:13.610
I've never been camping!

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:14.840
Then it's settled!

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:16.440
Don't just decide it like that.

00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:17.600
I'm in charge!

00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:19.410
And I'll talk to my aunt,

00:19:19.410 --> 00:19:22.570
so I can see Dr. Magata again!

00:19:23.820 --> 00:19:24.510
Alone.

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:28.210
Well? You're jealous, aren't you?

00:19:28.210 --> 00:19:30.710
She'll be right there, but you 
won't be able to see her.

00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:32.150
I'll go with you.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:33.760
Why?

00:19:33.760 --> 00:19:36.880
I don't want anything to happen to you.

00:19:38.770 --> 00:19:40.360
That isn't what you're thinking at all!

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:41.110
What do you think, Kunieda-kun?

00:19:42.680 --> 00:19:43.620
It's settled.

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:51.940
<i>1991, winter...</i>

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:55.410
<i>Since her parents were busy,</i>

00:19:55.410 --> 00:19:58.760
<i>she was sent to me far more often.</i>

00:20:02.290 --> 00:20:04.700
<i>She was always thinking...</i>

00:20:05.310 --> 00:20:07.300
<i>"What is life?</i>

00:20:08.030 --> 00:20:11.060
<i>It was always flashing.</i>

00:20:11.620 --> 00:20:14.400
<i>Flashing between life and death.</i>

00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:16.900
<i>What happens to a person after death?</i>

00:20:17.490 --> 00:20:18.780
<i>Does everything disappear?</i>

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:20.530
<i>Do you really think so?"</i>

00:20:21.580 --> 00:20:23.700
<i>When she asked me that,</i>

00:20:24.070 --> 00:20:26.090
<i>she was five.</i>

00:20:26.730 --> 00:20:29.020
<i>She was always thinking...</i>

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:31.230
<i>About who she was,</i>

00:20:31.230 --> 00:20:32.510
<i>where she'd come from,</i>

00:20:32.510 --> 00:20:34.040
<i>and where she was going.</i>

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:37.380
There was just one point in the conversation

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:39.170
when Dr. Magata seemed thrown off.

00:20:41.160 --> 00:20:42.390
Dr. Magata,

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:45.550
what was your motive for killing your parents?

00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:47.460
That is a stupid question.

00:20:47.930 --> 00:20:51.930
Do you really think there is any meaning 
in something like a motive?

00:20:52.530 --> 00:20:56.120
Did you come here to ask a thing like that?

00:20:58.230 --> 00:21:00.020
We're out of time.

00:21:00.340 --> 00:21:01.940
What is your last question?

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:07.200
Who are you?
